>HEAD

  DATAID="TON"
  ACQBY="AusMT test fixture"
  PROSPECT="Tipper-only fixture, no variances printed"
  LOC="Fixture"
  LAT=-34.750000
  LONG=139.500000
  EMPTY=1.0E+32

>INFO   MAXLINES=1000

  MINTED FIXTURE - NOT CUSTODIAN DATA. The same tipper-only shape as its
  sibling with one block fewer: the source prints no uncertainties, so
  TXVAR.EXP and TYVAR.EXP are OMITTED rather than fabricated and the written
  EMTF XML carries the missing-data sentinel in their place. That file still
  earns a variance entry in the statistical-estimate glossary, because the
  glossary names the estimate blocks the document contains. No byte is copied
  from any survey package: the identity is invented and the values are minted
  for this test.

>=DEFINEMEAS

  MAXCHAN=3
  MAXRUN=999
  MAXMEAS=99999
  UNITS=M
  REFTYPE=CART
  REFLAT=-34.750000
  REFLONG=139.500000

 >HMEAS ID= 1001.001 CHTYPE=HX X =  .000000  Y =  .000000  AZM=   0.0000
 >HMEAS ID= 1002.001 CHTYPE=HY X =  .000000  Y =  .000000  AZM=  90.0000
 >HMEAS ID= 1003.001 CHTYPE=HZ X =  .000000  Y =  .000000  AZM=  .000000

>=MTSECT
  SECTID=TON
  NFREQ=    5
  HX = 1001.001
  HY = 1002.001
  HZ = 1003.001

 >!****FREQUENCIES****!
 >FREQ NFREQ=   5  ORDER=DEC //    5
    0.20000E-02    0.10000E-02    0.50000E-03    0.25000E-03    0.12500E-03
 >!****TIPPER PARAMETERS****!
 >TXR.EXP ROT=0.0 //    5
   -0.40000E-01    0.70000E-01    0.11000E+00    0.22000E+00    0.34000E+00
 >TXI.EXP ROT=0.0 //    5
   -0.17000E+00   -0.19000E+00   -0.18000E+00   -0.16000E+00   -0.10000E+00
 >TYR.EXP ROT=0.0 //    5
    0.23000E+00    0.20000E+00    0.25000E+00    0.14000E+00    0.12000E+00
 >TYI.EXP ROT=0.0 //    5
   -0.20000E-01    0.20000E-01    0.90000E-01    0.90000E-01    0.50000E-01

>END
